            <div xml:id="d341">

                <pb facs="0355" n="290" sameAs="frus:frus1936v03/pg290"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.84/4515: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister Resident in Ethiopia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Engert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Addis
                                Ababa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-05-27T15:00:00+03:00">May 27, 1936—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 3:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>377. Regarding my 376 of today, please inform me whether foreigners residing in
                    Italy or Germany are expected to give respective national saltites. There would,
                    of course, be no objection to removing hats when passing national or regimental
                    colors or, as a matter of courtesy, even to Governor General but unless
                    instructed to the contrary I shall not advise Americans to give Fascist salute.
                    In any event I and my American staff have no intention of making any Roman
                    obeisances.</p>
                <pb facs="0356" n="291" xml:id="pg291"/>
                <p>The requirement to leave an automobile or get off a horse appears to me too
                    utterly ridiculous to be even dismissed.</p>
                <p>I shall confer with my diplomatic colleagues as soon as practicable.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Engert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
